@startuml Sequence Diagram - Successful Payment
title Escenario 1 - Pago Exitoso (Simulator API)
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 10
skinparam titleFontSize 11
skinparam ParticipantFontSize 10
skinparam ActorFontSize 10
skinparam ArrowFontSize 10
skinparam NoteFontSize 10
skinparam SequenceGroupFontSize 10
skinparam SequenceGroupHeaderFontSize 10
skinparam SequenceDividerFontSize 10
skinparam maxMessageSize 95
hide footbox
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam ArrowColor #666666
skinparam LifeLineBorderColor #666666

participant "Comercio\n(Backend)" as Comercio
participant "SDK KitPagos" as SDK
participant "Simulator API\n(Fastify)" as SimAPI
participant "GatewayMockFactory" as MockFactory
participant "TransactionStore" as Store

Comercio -> SDK : createPayment(\nCreatePaymentRequest)
SDK -> SimAPI : POST /v1/sim/{gateway}/payments\n(Auth + Body nativo de la pasarela)
SimAPI -> MockFactory : buildApprovedResponse(\ngateway, request)
MockFactory -> MockFactory : Genera payload nativo\n(Wompi: {data:{id,\nstatus:"APPROVED"}},\nMercado Pago: {id,\nstatus:"approved"},\nRapyd: {data:{id,\nstatus:"CLO",paid:true}},\nKushki: {ticketNumber,\ndetails:{transactionStatus:\n"APPROVAL"}})
MockFactory -> Store : save(\ngatewayTransactionId,\npayload)
Store --> MockFactory : OK
MockFactory --> SimAPI : payload nativo
SimAPI --> SDK : HTTP 201 / 200 (payload nativo)
SDK -> SDK : ResponseNormalizer.\nnormalize(payload,\ngateway)
SDK --> Comercio : PaymentResult(\nTRANSACTION:\nstatus=APPROVED)

note over Comercio, Store
  Para Wompi (punto 50): el simulador crea en PENDING y resuelve a APPROVED en la
  primera consulta de estado, reflejando el comportamiento asincrono de la pasarela
  real. Para Mercado Pago con PSE: devuelve REDIRECT_REQUIRED con redirectUrl; la
  consulta posterior por el id ORD... devuelve APPROVED. Para Rapyd con tarjeta:
  devuelve REDIRECT_REQUIRED al hosted checkout; simula el pago y la consulta
  devuelve APPROVED.
end note

@enduml
